above gives\n\n$$\n0=\\frac{3}{2}({0}^{2})+C\\,⟹\\,C=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.$ In particular, its inital velocity at time $t=1\\,s$ and final velocity at time $t=2\\,s$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{0} & =v(1)=\\frac{3}{2}({1}^{2})=\\frac{3}{2}\\,m/s, \\\\ {v}_{1} & =v(2)=\\frac{3}{2}({2}^{2})=6\\,m/s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change in kinetic energy of the particle between these times is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ\\,\\text{KE} & =\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}\\cdot {6}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{5}-\\frac{9}{5} \\\\  & =27\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319921 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319922 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319923 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319924 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319925 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1041 "selection" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319925 13194139534919 true] [17592186319920 1110 #uuid "76f1e80b-03d7-53d7-abe3-1ba9f0dda61a" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319921 1034 "12\\,J" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534919 true] [17592186319921 1111 #uuid "0f540567-b661-5bca-8f06-ce7188bb3bef" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319922 1034 "16\\,J" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534919 true] [17592186319922 1111 #uuid "b3f00337-993c-58a0-939a-72a28200cffe" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319923 1034 "24\\,J" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534919 true] [17592186319923 1111 #uuid "f1ad6484-6f17-5a7c-99e6-71ee26604b37" 13194139534919 true] [17592186319924 1